        "section": [
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">COPD exacerbation, treated with bronchodilators and steroids</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "67781-5",
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Summarization of encounter note"
                }
              ]
            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the recent hospital admission of your 84-year-old male patient, admitted on 28/02/2010 due to an acute exacerbation of his known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD). On admission, clinical examination revealed significant dyspnoea, prolonged expiration, and reduced oxygen saturation. Arterial blood gas analysis confirmed hypoxaemic respiratory insufficiency. Chest X-ray showed pulmonary hyperinflation without signs of pneumonia or cardiac decompensation. ECG excluded acute cardiac events. The patient was treated with supplemental oxygen therapy, nebulised bronchodilators (salbutamol and ipratropium), systemic corticosteroids, and intravenous fluids. Vital signs were monitored continuously. Under this treatment, the patient's condition improved satisfactorily. He was discharged on 01/03/2010 in stable condition. Inhaled maintenance therapy and oral corticosteroid taper were prescribed. Follow-up in your practice within one week is recommended. Please do not hesitate to contact me for further information.</div>"
            },
